    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "BOARD DECK TEMPLATE",
      "color": "#FFFFFF",
      "fontFamily": "Open Sans SemiBold"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "When a company starts to run board meetings, among the first question are usually those about the board pack: The material delivered to the board members prior to the meeting. ",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "color": "#FFFFFF",
      "fontFamily": "Open Sans"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "The board deck should help structure the meeting, document the status of the company and foster discussions and decisions the management wants the board to make. And clear the path ahead for the CEO.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "color": "#FFFFFF",
      "fontFamily": "Open Sans"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "This deck was designed to help you set up your first board deck to achieve all that. A board deck is a living, breathing organism, which will be re-defined again and again as your company grows. This template will ensure you don’t start at zero.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "color": "#FFFFFF",
      "fontFamily": "Open Sans"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "Copy it, change it, use it.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "color": "#FFFFFF",
      "fontFamily": "Open Sans"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
      "content": "\n"
    },
    {
